{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/293005-detect-avernian-gate-anyone","id":293005,"title":"Detect Avernian Gate, anyone?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-26T09:51:15-07:00","id":293005,"title":"Detect Avernian Gate, anyone?","content":"Hi guys and gals. I was hoping that someone here could help me out. I am afraid that I am completely overlooking something that ought to be obvious, of course, but I have not, anywhere, been able to find information about how a Sin-Eater can find/detect/locate an Avernian Gate. Not in the Geist Core Book, not on the Internet. Nowhere. Book of The Dead contains information about how other denizens of the WoD can detect a Gateway, but NOT how a Sin-Eater does it. If at all. But seriously, can you pass by an unmarked Avernian Gate at say three feet (or 300 or whatever) without sensing that its there? It's all well and good, that The Twilight Network keeps a record of sorts of neraby Gates in a given location. But they must have been able to FIND them in the first place, right? I find it improbable (and more than a little annoying) that a Sin-Eater should be unable to detect a hitherto unknown Gate, while to a Mage with the Death arcanum its a walk in the park. And if a Gateway is located somewhere in the London Underground but is unmarked so as not to make it too easy for those pesky sorcerers and lycanthropes, then HOW do you locate just the RIGHT deadend (or stretch of wall or whatever) where the Avernian Gate IS? I am a little puzzled, I admit, so if someone hee would be so kind as to point me in the right direction, it would be very helpful :-)<br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4161-lhune","name":"Lhune","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:25:53-07:00","id":293077,"title":"","content":"Underworld Gates exist in the ghostly frequency of Twilight, so Sin Eaters should be able to see them innately if they pass by. The Stigmata Boneyard also allows them to sense any passages to the Underworld (with only the first dot even). I might also allow the geist to whisper about nearby gates if its relevant to the plot or its agenda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:56:24-07:00","id":293107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/293005-detect-avernian-gate-anyone?p=293077#post293077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Underworld Gates exist in the ghostly frequency of Twilight, so Sin Eaters should be able to see them innately if they pass by. The Stigmata Boneyard also allows them to sense any passages to the Underworld (with only the first dot even). I might also allow the geist to whisper about nearby gates if its relevant to the plot or its agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, great. Thanks :-) I had not considered that Gates exist &quot;in Twilight&quot;, as it were. Makes sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4161-lhune","name":"Lhune","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T06:56:48-07:00","id":293702,"title":"","content":"I'd also argue that they're not a specific 'door' so to speak. They are locations - opening them might make a door manifest, but it's also possible that a cenote has 2-3 different arches that can be used as the same door if someone were to open it.<br /> <br /> As an example to illustrate the wacky logic in my greybits - imagine a cenote in a hallway. There are dozens of doorways that can be used as the actual passageway, so when you open the door one of them will become the literal passageway. But which one actually opens? Depends on the person opening the door: which one do they EXPECT to open? The fact of the matter is that wooden frame of the door isn't the passageway - the whole area is. The door frame just acts as that doorways manifestation in the physical realm.<br /> <br /> This actually gives me an idea - what if someone used this sort of logic to trick someone into the underworld rather than leaving a cenote to go home? Perhaps have them stumble into a domain that seems like the regular world and have them not initially catch on that they're in the underworld....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}